@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-10
@reviewed: 2026-06-10

Feature: Target Diagnostics
  "Read-only diagnostics for a Mason target: SSH reachability, remote permissions, manifest access, HTTP privacy probes, symlink serving, and Caddy reconcile."

  Provides:
    - setup.Diagnose @source("symbol:Diagnose")
    - setup.DoctorDeps @source("symbol:DoctorDeps")
    - setup.DoctorReport @source("symbol:DoctorReport")
    - setup.DoctorCheck @source("symbol:DoctorCheck")
    - setup.CheckStatus @source("symbol:CheckStatus")

  Consumes:
    - config.Target
    - remote.CommandRunner
    - remote.ManifestStore
    - domain.Manifest
    - domain.ObjectURL
    - domain.SlugURL

  Invariants:
    - Diagnose MUST stay read-only and never mutate remote state
    - Probe failures MUST become fail or warn checks, not returned errors
    - DoctorReport.Healthy MUST tolerate warnings and fail only when a check status is fail
    - HTTP probes MUST verify /.mason/manifest.json and /objects/ are not publicly reachable (200)
    - Symlink serving MUST GET a manifest-backed slug or object-path URL and fail on non-2xx
    - An empty manifest or no enabled endpoints MUST warn and skip the symlink probe, not fail
    - When manifest fetch fails, the symlink probe MUST warn as skipped rather than misreport
    - Caddy reconcile via the admin API MUST be best-effort: unreachable API yields warn on both host and root checks
    - For an apex-domain target, Caddy reconcile MUST additionally check the www→apex redirect host and warn (not fail) when it is absent
    - Remote rsync availability MUST be verified on the server

  OutOfScope:
    - Local onboarding and config writes (setup.Run)
    - Remote bootstrap script generation (RemoteInitScript)
    - Unmanifested symlink drift detection and blob orphan audits
    - Multi-target config editing (target subcommands, M-073)

  Scenario (happy-path): Healthy target
    Given SSH, writable trees, a readable manifest with an enabled endpoint, private prefixes, and matching Caddy config
    When Diagnose runs
    Then every critical check is ok and DoctorReport.Healthy is true

  Scenario (happy-path): Fresh empty manifest
    Given a reachable server with an empty manifest and no shares yet
    When Diagnose runs
    Then manifest is ok and symlink serving warns with no enabled endpoints while the report stays healthy

  Scenario (negative): Public manifest leak
    Given HTTP GET on /.mason/manifest.json returns 200
    When Diagnose runs
    Then the private-prefix check fails and DoctorReport.Healthy is false

  Scenario (negative): Symlink not served
    Given a manifest with an enabled slug and HTTP GET on that URL returns 404
    When Diagnose runs
    Then symlink serving fails and DoctorReport.Healthy is false

  Scenario (edge): Caddy admin unavailable
    Given SSH works but localhost:2019 is unreachable
    When Diagnose runs
    Then both Caddy checks warn and DoctorReport.Healthy remains true

  Scenario (edge): Apex domain missing www redirect
    Given an apex-domain target whose Caddy config has no www host
    When Diagnose runs
    Then a www-redirect check warns with site-init and www-DNS guidance while the report stays healthy
